# Design System

All tokens are defined once in `src/app/globals.css`. Light is canonical; `.dark`
overrides the same variable names, and `@theme inline` maps them to Tailwind.

## Never hardcode a colour

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — breaks dark mode, invisible to the token system
<div className="bg-[#edeae2] text-[#16171a] border-[#d6d1c6]">

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="bg-paper text-ink border-line">
```

Semantic tokens: `paper`, `paper-raised`, `paper-sunk`, `ink`, `mist`, `whisper`,
`line`, `line-strong`, `pine` (accent), `ember` (errors only).

Adding a colour means adding it in three places — `:root`, `.dark`, and
`@theme inline`. A token that only exists in one theme is a bug.

## Type

- `font-display` (Newsreader serif) for headings and pull quotes, always `font-light`.
- `font-sans` (Archivo) for body copy.
- `label` / `label-sm` utilities for every micro-caption: mono, uppercase, wide tracking.
  Use the utility, don't re-declare `text-xs uppercase tracking-widest`.
- `wordmark` utility for the extended-grotesk name treatment (uses Archivo's width axis).

Display sizes come from the `@theme` scale: `text-mega`, `text-display`, `text-title`,
`text-lead`. Reach for those before writing an arbitrary `text-[...]` clamp.

## Layout rhythm

- `gutter` for horizontal page padding, `pt-section` for vertical section spacing.
- `rule-t` / `rule-b` for hairlines; `RuleLine` when it should draw itself in on scroll.
- Every top-level section opens with `<SectionHeader index="0X" kicker="..." />`.
